projects.description:
2021: Capacity building to prepare the country for large scale immunization
2022: Capacity building to prepare the country for large scale immunization, implementation of behavioral insight studies, support of vaccination communication and awareness raising activities, further support for digitalization of immunization; services and monitoring of adverse effects, monitoring and evaluation of vaccination practices etc; 
In 2023:  Continues support of SARI study - Study for COVID-19 Vaccine effectiveness in preventing SARI hospitalizations associated with COVID-19 infection. North Macedonia has joined this network to contribute to the critical information to predict future COVID-19 activity and its impact on SARI patients; Support central/sub- central authorities in identifying or devising appropriate platform(s) and service delivery mechanisms to deliver COVID-19 vaccines to target population groups as per the central vaccination strategy with minimal disruptions to the routine immunization services; Capacity building for the newly established vaccination service delivery modalities (mobile teams, teams for vaccinating at elderly homes, pharmacies, clinical departments etc) with expanding the scope of the existing immunization programme mechanisms which can be used in the future to strengthen routine immunization services;  Develop and adapt officially the vaccinator supervision and competency assessment tool – with focus on COVID-19 vaccinators; Support central /sub- central authorities in defining essential data and indicators needed to monitor immunization performance;  Updating the Immunization Rulebook; Continuation of micro planning activities at the district and health facility level using the RED strategy in North Macedonia; Capacity building of all HCWs in vaccination units on Vaccination Best Practices; Continuation of the process for establishment of an institutionalized system to gather and use behavioral and social data for planning and evaluation of the demand for Covid-19 vaccines;  Developing and implementing a plan for risk communication and community engagement interventions for increased trust and uptake of COVID-19 vaccination as well as COVID-19 prevention behaviors, especially for at-risk population, with the support of NGOs and associations and municipalities;  Digitization of the cold chain surveillance system in vaccination points; Develop and distribute IPC-related print or electronic communication materials for health facilities, schools, and other institutions and in high-risk communities; Conduct campaigns incorporating IPC messaging to promote COVID-19 protective hygiene practices; Design and implement evidence-based communication for development initiatives to address vaccine hesitancy and generate demand for immunization [routine immunization; Technical support to strengthen coordination, planning and implementation of the national Government-led COVID-19 vaccine related communication and community engagement activities; Generating evidence to inform the design, implementation and evaluation of social and behavior change communication and vaccine demand generation activities; Supporting evidence-based multi-media campaigns and community engagement activities to address barriers to vaccine up-take, including development, testing and dissemination of tailored messages through various media; Strengthening the capacity of journalists to engage in factual reporting around COVID-19 vaccines and providing support to establish formal systems for misinformation management; 
In 2024:  Technical guidance, support in capacity building, increasing awareness about immunization benefits, Finalising a new immunization rulebook, promoting digitalization in immunization, supporting the National Immunization Technical Advisory Group, Continues support of SARI study - Study for COVID-19 Vaccine effectiveness in preventing SARI hospitalizations associated with COVID-19 infection, Continuation of micro planning activities at the district and health facility level using the RED strategy in North Macedonia ; 
UNICEF: Support the Ministry of Health to develop the National Immunisation Strategy; Advocacy and technical support to Ministry of Health to implement policy recommendations for strengthening misinformation management on immunisation; 
2025: WHO: Future steps include strengthening the implementation of the new Immunization rulebook, enhancing cross-sector collaboration to integrate immunization data across healthcare providers, launching a new reporting system for vaccine-preventable diseases, and focusing on innovative approaches to reach underserved communities and sustain high immunization coverage.
UNICEF: Finalization of the National Immunization Strategy 2030 and revision of the methodology for calculation of vaccination coverage rates. Digitalization of inter-personal skills on immunization modules and their inclusion as mandatory for medical graduates

In 2021: support to the PHC reform process
In 2022: Advocate with high level PHC stakeholders on the importance of the process of reform of PHC (including gynecologists and pediatricians), provide technical guidance on quality performance monitoring, support of technical workshops for development of PHC protocols and indicators, support assessment of legislative needs and identify follow up steps, support raising awareness of patients for the new PHC reform. Support development of Pediatric care masterplan 2030 with costed action plan for reorganization of the levels of care; Functional analysis of the home visiting system with recommendations to strengthen their role, revision of existing modules for community care, development of SOPs for the work of patronage nurses, unification of their competencies and establishment of supportive supervision system); Research to understand demand bottlenecks to inform strategy to increase demand and quality of home visiting services; Develop COVID-19 detection, monitoring and response-focused modules to be incorporated in the existing e-health system known as “Moj termin” to broaden access to health professionals at primary, secondary and tertiary levels of healthcare (including development of national guidelines for detection, assessment and treatment of COVID-19 patients through primary healthcare); Mainstreaming ACEs screening into primary healthcare; 
Situation analysis of early childhood intervention services; Survey of mental health disorders in pregnant women and the perinatal period, to assess consequences of COVID-19 in pregnant women and mothers with newborns, and put forward proposals for improved response; 
In 2023: Technical support to the design and implementation of a Hypertension Initiative in one demonstration site;  
Technical support to the development of the Master plan for Primary health Care for North Macedonia; Ensure continuity of the PHC restructuring plans according to the adopted renewed model of PHC; Technical support to the roll out of the PHC protocols (training of primary health care professionals); 
Technical support to the design and roll out of digital tools in PHC (e-appointments and PHC dashboards);
Technical support for assessment of the Agency for accreditation and quality of health institutions and awareness raising for patient safety; Development of national patient safety plan and Action plan for strengthening of the Agency for accreditation and quality of health institutions; Implementation of training packages in the area of patient safety for hospital managers and hospital staff; 
In 2024: Continuation of activities initiated in 2023; Development and implementation of training programme for primary care nurses for health promotion and disease prevention as per the newly introduced protocols; Support in implementation of the National Patient Safety Action Plan; Support of patient safety initiatives in pilot selected hospitals; 
UNICEF: Support the introduced digital solutions for quality improvement and enhanced accountability in primary healthcare; Advocacy and technical support to the Ministry of Health, Health Insurance Fund and regional healthcare centres to implement policy recommendations for strengthening immunization and home-visiting services; 
In 2025: Assisting the Ministry of Health in establishing a robust governance structure and coordination mechanisms to effectively lead and manage the PHC reform.
Further refining the new PHC service delivery model to ensure it meets the evolving needs of communities and aligns with international best practices.
Supporting the MoH in piloting the new PHC service delivery model, providing technical guidance to inform its successful implementation and adaptation.
Collaborating with the MoH to develop a comprehensive PHC Masterplan, which will outline a strategic framework for sustainable PHC services, resource allocation, and capacity building across the health sector.
These efforts aim to build a cohesive, community-focused PHC system that strengthens the country’s healthcare foundation and contributes to universal health coverage.
UNICEF: Home visiting maturity assessment with recommendations for optimal functioning to reach most vulnerable mothers and children, establishment of a professional organization (Nurses Chamber), licensing and re-licensing of nurses, Fiscal space analysis to identify sources of funding to ensure sustainability and high-quality of home-visiting and other preventive healthcare services

2021: Advocacy activities to promote prevention

2022: Supporting the finalization of the Clinical Guidelines on Prevention and Early Detection of Cervical Cancer;
Strengthened advocacy and communication with the general public on the available tools and resources for prevention of cervical cancer – vaccination and screening;
Support to the introduction of HPV-based testing, and its gradual rollout on national level, vis-a-vis the traditional PAP test, given the medical science evidence in support of the HPV-based testing
Increasing the coverage with Cervical Cancer screening, with focus on women and girls in rural areas, and women and girls from marginalized communities, through mobile gynecological clinics

In 2022: Technical packages to address risk factors of Noncommunicable diseases and their risk factors through multi-sectoral action (obesity, physical activity, fat and sugary drinks taxation, trans - fat elimination and salt reduction); Capacity building for NCDs Risk factor surveillance (STEPS); NCDs programme capacity building for mid - level managers in public health; Assessment related to the WHO Initiative on Trans fats elimination and salt reduction in line with new EU resolution, support implementation of the physical activity portfolio of MoH and the Government; Support to COSI; 

In 2023: Technical support for implementation of activities related to tobacco control, specifically strengthening of cessation services, advocacy for creating tobacco - free zones and awareness raising of the adverse effects of tobacco; Technical support for development of national strategy for trans - fat elimination; Advocacy for endorsement and support for implementation of the Action Plan on Salt Reduction; Supporting awareness raising about physical activity at work - space. 

In 2024: Technical support for implementation of activities related to tobacco control, specifically implementation of tobacco investment case, implementation of behavioral insight study for the barriers and drivers for tobacco cessation; Technical support for development of national programme on physical activity at work place; Technical support for implementation of the Action Plan on Salt Reduction; Capacity building for NCDs Risk factor surveillance (STEPS); 
Evidence generation on the main drivers of childhood obesity. 
UNICEF: Support the Ministry of Health and other national and sub-national stakeholders to address the trends in child and adolescents' obesity; Advocacy and capacity building for healthcare providers on International Classification of Functioning, Disability and Health

In 2025: WHO: Technical support for the endorsement and implementation of national protocols for tobacco cessation in primary healthcare (PHC) and standard operating procedures (SOPs) for Public Health Centers; Support for the revision of the Tobacco Control Law and the development of a new law, ensuring it is informed by comprehensive consultations before submission for Government endorsement; Assistance in raising awareness and promoting initiatives for effective tobacco control.

